{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Round-2 plan review BLOCKed with 4 blocking findings (sidecar reviewed_at 1793599775757466775, job 1793599449483502381-...). All 4 remediated in the plan just written back (7,997 chars, under the 8,000 admission cap):\n\n1. **Uncited surfacing sibling (G1G2, impact 1.0).** Correct. The ACs asserting \"the create exits 0\" and \"the advisory\" rest on a create-path consumer of `find_similar` that does not exist on origin/main, and the ticket's only `depends_on` was 47c8 — the *index* sibling, whose own plan says siblings add the advisory. The surfacing sibling is 80a5-cbb1-ef06-4ba5 (pinelike-wayfaring-sanderling), now cited inline as `the create advisory across the four surfaces [rebar:80a5-cbb1-ef06-4ba5]`, alongside `the index sibling [rebar:47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88]`.\n\n   **The `depends_on -> 80a5` edge is deliberately NOT added yet.** 80a5 is `in_progress`, not closed, so declaring the edge now would make this ticket \"open but blocked by an unclosed dependency\" and `review-plan` would fast-fail with an unsigned INDETERMINATE before spending an LLM call. The edge goes in immediately after 80a5 closes, and the re-review runs then. This is the documented review-dependencies-first ordering, not a deferral of the fix.\n\n2. **Index validity key ignores model identity (G6, impact 1.0).** Correct and a real defect: both model strings are operator-overridable, so a changed embedding model would have left stale vectors — possibly of a different dimensionality — in a dir-hash-keyed index and ranked cosine similarity across incompatible spaces. New Approach paragraph (\"Stored vectors are keyed by what produced them\") folds the embedding-model identity and the pinned digest-prompt commit into the validity key, plus a new AC asserting the affected entries are re-embedded rather than reused.\n\n3. **AC2's no-skip guarantee rested on an unpinned install (T3, impact 1.0).** The finding's premise is that `pydantic_ai.embeddings.openai` did not import in the gate environment. Measured in this checkout's venv, all 4 of `pydantic_ai.embeddings`, `.bedrock`, `.openai` and `.test` import — so the gate env is not a dev install. The underlying gap is still real: the plan asserted the no-skip property without naming what guarantees it. It is already guaranteed — `pydantic-ai-slim[openai]` (pyproject.toml:310) and `pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock]` (:313) are both declared in the `dev` extra, carrying the explicit rationale \"present here so its tests RUN in CI rather than skipping\". The plan now cites those two lines and requires the test to FAIL rather than skip when a backend is absent. No dependency list changes, so AC \"rebar's declared dependencies are unchanged\" stays true.\n\n4. **No discriminator between the two digest failure states (T8, impact 1.0).** Correct — the plan handled them oppositely (retry vs. count-and-fall-back) while giving no rule to classify a reply. Defined now by whether a digest object was recovered at all: a reply yielding no JSON- or YAML-decodable mapping carrying any of the 4 fields is \"did not answer the task\" and is retried once; a reply where a mapping IS recovered but every field is empty is the empties state, which increments the counter and falls back with no retry. The three shapes ADR 0122 names (`ticket_digest` wrapper key, YAML instead of JSON, JSON behind a prose preamble) all recover a mapping, so they land in the empties branch; the observed non-answer (a model that began performing the ticket's refactoring work) recovers none. AC-8 through AC-10 were reworded to that predicate.\n\nTwo near-duplicate ACs (provider denial, provider timeout) were merged into one parameterized AC to stay under the admission cap.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793601145659418113,"uuid":"201e8f07-50aa-4791-9196-39221fe72d05"}